  "description": "The corner's a <= b chain simulated in the LIST model Lean actually uses (AlgElement.ofTerms L, every lemma reading its redex off L1 ++ (W, c) :: L2 and so needing W to occur exactly once), rather than the confluence engine's cleaned word -> coefficient map. The two agree until the prefix's mid-way cancellation, where two terms reconverge on one word with opposite coefficients: the engine drops both, the list keeps both. Measured: the dead pair is never rewritten (dup_sources = 0), so on that count it could be carried -- but it leaves 4 entries at T_pre against the 2 tailChain is stated on, and ONE of the dead words extends a live term's block context, which is exactly what blockPass's hpark forbids. So ofTerms_cancel_pair is FORCED, not by any word being reduced twice (this arc's earlier guess) but by hpark being a condition on every other entry, live or dead. Nothing new is needed to discharge it: Basic.lean §6 already has SingleStepReduction.of_coeffEq_left and MultiStepReduction.congr_source.",
